completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in 4.7.stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.stable - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 4 monitors - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3070 Ti (NVIDIA; 32.0.16.1062) - AMD Ryzen 7 9700X 8-Core Processor (16 threads) - 31.16 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen enabling a `Shader Preview` on a line **after** setting a shader built-in output variable, such as `ROUGHNESS =` or `NORMAL_MAP = ` will show the properties that have been set to the material on the preview, even when the assignment that is previewed is unrelated.\n\n<img width=\"1806\" height=\"1392\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0454ce97-51f7-49d5-8c63-234f8ac4ad1b\" />\n\nThis results in the preview image **not representing the actual data that is being assigned on the line that is previewed**, which is an issue.\n\nThe only properties that don't have this issue seems to be `ALBEDO` and `ALPHA`, since it likely overwrites those completely.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open a shader\n2. Set the `NORMAL_MAP` to a texture or something obviously visible.\n3. Create a standalone assignment line for a variable, and place it after the `NORMAL_MAP` line. Something like `float test = 0.0` or `vec3 test = vec3(1.0, 0.0, 0.0) will do.\n4. Preview the line.\n5. The preview will show the current state of the material, which includes `NORMAL_MAP` and similar properties, on top of the data assigned by the previewed line.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121741/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121741/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}